From: Andrei Gosman <andrei.gosman@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH 025/NNN] rf_uhd: lower the default master clock rate for LibreSDR B220

The LibreSDR B220 mini identifies itself as a B200 series device, so it
takes the 23.04 MHz default, but it is not one. It runs the stock B210
bitstream on different silicon, an Artix-7 XC7A200T, and loses its VITA
control channel above roughly 11.52 MHz.

Measured on one unit: 11.52 stable, 15.36 and 23.04 and 30.72 all fail in
wait_for_ack. At 11.52 the device is good for PSS, SSS and MIB at 1.92
MSps, which is what cell search needs; a 20 MHz cell decodes only
partially.

Deliberately not proposed upstream. A genuine Ettus B210 handles 61.44
without trouble, so lowering the default there would cost those users
bandwidth for no reason. This belongs in the macOS fork, where the LibreSDR
is the hardware in use. A B210 owner can restore the upstream default with
master_clock_rate=23.04e6 in device_args, and the code comment says so.

diff --git a/lib/src/phy/rf/rf_uhd_imp.cc b/lib/src/phy/rf/rf_uhd_imp.cc
index f1ad4df9a..72834aa73 100644
--- a/lib/src/phy/rf/rf_uhd_imp.cc
+++ b/lib/src/phy/rf/rf_uhd_imp.cc
@@ -701,7 +701,16 @@ static int uhd_init(rf_uhd_handler_t* handler, char* args, uint32_t nof_channels
   // Parse/Select master clock rate
   if (not device_addr.has_key("master_clock_rate") and device_addr.has_key("type")) {
     // Default master clock rate for B200 series
-    std::string mcr = "23.04e6";
+    // Lowered from 23.04e6 for LibreSDR B220 mini, which presents itself as a
+    // B200 series device but runs the stock B210 bitstream on different
+    // silicon and loses its VITA control channel above this rate. Measured on
+    // one unit: 11.52 stable, 15.36 and 23.04 and 30.72 all fail in
+    // wait_for_ack. Enough for PSS, SSS and MIB at 1.92 MSps; a 20 MHz cell
+    // decodes only partially.
+    //
+    // A genuine Ettus B210 is unaffected and can be put back on the upstream
+    // default with master_clock_rate=23.04e6 in device_args.
+    std::string mcr = "11.52e6";
 
     if (device_addr["type"] == "x300") {
       mcr = "184.32e6";
